The goal of this project is to&nbsp;envision in which direction a platform like Forvo could evolve, from its current standpoint, in order to offer a richer user experience.

To move toward this goal, I started by looking at Forvo’s position as a platform, and what it&nbsp;could&nbsp;aim for. These observations are speculative – I didn’t work with the team, and their accuracy isn’t the point: they are meant to provide context for the design decisions I made.

The goal was not merely to redesign the UI based on existing pain points; instead, I aimed to explore the&nbsp;broader potential of the platform: understanding how it could better support users, engage the community, and create a more seamless and meaningful interaction with words and pronunciations. This meant looking at the app as a living ecosystem, considering not just screens and buttons, but&nbsp;how users discover, learn, and contribute content, and, ultimately, how the platform could grow to meet both current and future needs.
